    <briefdescription>
<para>The Composite Guidance Law encompasses a sequence of one or more guidance laws to be used over specific time intervals. At each point in time, the applicable guidance law is selected and used to calculate the thrust acceleration. Guidance laws don&apos;t need to be contiguous, and can be added in any order. If the instant does not fall within any of the intervals, the thrust acceleration is zero. The guidance law intervals must not intersect each other. </para>
    </briefdescription>
